q3_ui Video Mode list for the retro-agent fleet (baseq3/zz-fleetres-ui.pk3)

Applies to code/q3_ui/ui_video.c of id Software's GPL Quake III Arena source,
github.com/id-Software/Quake-III-Arena @ dbe4ddb10315479fc00086f08e25d968b4b43c49
- the tree that rebuilds baseq3/pak8.pk3 vm/ui.qvm (1.32) byte-for-byte, md5
3e6b8fadb2a970c2b754e48e63a054d7 (see apply.py).  Needs ui_fleetres.h (beside
this file) copied into code/q3_ui/.  Built, checked and packaged by apply.py
in this directory.  GPL-2.0-or-later, as the source it modifies.

What changes: the Video Mode spin control lists r_availableModes when the
engine publishes it (ioquake3) and id's 12-mode table otherwise (retail
1.32c); the mode the game is running in (r_mode -1 = r_customwidth x
r_customheight) is always listed and selected; ACCEPT with that entry writes
the running mode back unchanged, any other entry is written as id's r_mode
for id's sizes and as r_mode -1 + r_customwidth/r_customheight otherwise.
Nothing else in the UI changes.

